Ported from ../outln/__tests__/cases/walker/032-glob-respects-gitignore.case.yaml; expected output is the TypeScript build's.
Its source-code inputs were rewritten as Markdown files.
input/.git/HEAD makes input a git repository: outln applies .gitignore files only inside one.
Except: the glob view says "a header or summary" instead of "header comments" (docs/changelog.md).
== args
input/**/*.md
== file input/.git/HEAD
ref: refs/heads/main
== file input/.gitignore
dist/
!dist/keep.md
*.gen.md
== file input/src/a.md
---
description: Source a.
---
# a
== file input/src/a.gen.md
---
description: Generated.
---
# gen
== file input/dist/out.md
---
description: Dist output.
---
# out
== file input/dist/keep.md
---
description: Cannot be re-included: parent dist/ is excluded.
---
# keep
== file input/node_modules/dep/index.md
---
description: Dependency.
---
# dep
== stdout
glob view: input/**/*.md
Includes only a header or summary per file.
For file-level outlines, use `outln [FILE]...`.
